Majority Element
Exercise

Given an integer array nums, find the element that appears more than n / 2 times.

You may assume that such an element always exists.

Examples:

nums = [3, 2, 3]

Output: 3
nums = [2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2]

Output: 2


Solution:

1. The standard solution using Map

const nums = [3, 2, 3];
let map = new Map();
let output = 0;

for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
  map.set(nums[i], (map.get(nums[i]) || 0) + 1);
}

for (let [key, value] of map) {
  if (value > nums.length / 2) {
    output = key;
  }
}

console.log(output);


2. Boyer–Moore Majority Vote algorithm.

Solution:

const nums = [3, 2, 3];
let candidate = 0;
let count = 0;

for (let i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
  if (count === 0) {
    candidate = nums[i];
  }

  if (nums[i] === candidate) {
    count += 1;
  } else {
    count -= 1;
  }
}

console.log(candidate);
